      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. but i'm worried some of the more traditional board members might push back. they'll probably argue that we have a fiduciary duty to maximize profits for shareholders above everything else, and that shifting focus to social goals is basically just politics or a distraction from making money. \n\nhow should i address that specific concern in the memo? i want to show them why the 'fiduciary duty' argument doesn't actually mean we should ignore ESG.",
